[Music]  i am brayden hamilton and i am the  founder of orca asphalt maintenance  one of our primary services is asphalt  sealcoating i'm going to walk you  through how we clean repair and seal  an asphalt driveway  so typically when we show up on a  project we assess the driveway and we  see cracks  now cracks are inevitable over time  asphalt moves and typically what we see  is cracks down the seams of the asphalt  which could be in the center of the  driveway or where the driveway meets the  road so before we start our sealcoating  project there is a lot of dirt and  debris grime oils that need to be  cleaned off the reason for this is we  want our sealer to properly adhere to  the asphalt  after the driveway is cleaned we then  use an oil spot primer on any spots  where oil has been leaked from out of  cars or motorcycles this oil spot primer  is poured on the spot and then applied  with a broom to work it in this ensures  that the oil doesn't penetrate through  and that our sealer is able to stick on  that surface  crack sealing is an essential part of  the process as it prevents water from  penetrating into the asphalt that water  can wash away the base which will  eventually lead to asphalt failure the  asphalt on top can cave in and potholes  can form and much worse issues can arise  we begin the repair by ensuring that  crack is perfectly clean and then we use  our push behind melters which melt a  rubber compound it comes out of the  machine through a spout and into the  shoe which is then walked along the  crack filling the void  this rubber compound is formulated to  expand and contract with the thermal  expansion of the asphalt  typically one pass is needed but if that  crack is large we need to go over top of  that crack several times to ensure it's  properly sealed  in the winter months the asphalt will  contract leaving a larger void in that  asphalt and in the summer it expands  leaving the cracks smaller we want a  compound that can get in there and  expand and contract with that crack  ensuring that it doesn't open up and  further moisture can penetrate  the push behind melter is heated to 350  degrees celsius which is the perfect  temperature for the rubber to come out  of the machine and fill the crack at a  perfect consistency  now that we're done repairing the cracks  we're going to move on to seal coating  the driveway  seal coating protects from salt uv rays  water penetration and many other  contaminants  we use a professional-grade asphalt  emulsion sealer that has compounds that  ensure that it's durable and non-slip  so in a residential setting we use  specialized seal coating brooms so the  product is applied in lines and then we  come behind with brooms sweeping it back  and forth working that sealer into the  asphalt pores  seal coating a driveway is a little bit  like a dance so we've got typically two  people on a project and we are working  it back and forth pulling it down on the  edges working our edges and then working  the middle all at the same time so that  it cures in beautifully  so our sealer is housed in a tank we  have a pump that pumps it out of the  tank through a hose and out of a wand  through this wand comes the sealer and  it is applied in lines and then we come  behind with brooms and we work that  sealer back and forth back and forth  working it into the pores and leaving a  perfect finish  so when the sealer is applied it has a  brown color and it cures to a jet black  we chalk line a perfect line at the end  of the driveways and then we mask it off  so that when we pull the sealer onto the  masking paper and pull it up at the end  customers are left with a perfect line  it will typically take between three and  four hours to walk on the driveway but  we always recommend 24 to 48 hours prior  to driving  we recommend that driveways are seal  coated every three to four years we  recommend getting this process done in  the summer months as the temperatures  allow it to cure properly and fast

